title: 'eth-rpc: keep the sync head behind un-indexed subscription gaps'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    The subscription gap filler no longer lets the `sync-head` label advance over blocks it failed to index. Previously a gap fill that errored, or a gap dropped because the gap queue was full, still counted as done, so the head moved past the missing blocks and a restart never filled them. `eth_getLogs` and `eth_getBlockReceipts` then returned incomplete results for those blocks. A finalized block whose own processing failed was skipped the same way; it is now handed to the gap filler like a missed block.

    A failed gap fill is now attempted up to 3 times, waiting 2 and then 4 seconds between attempts. In archive mode (`--eth-pruning=archive`) a gap that still fails, or that did not fit in the queue, keeps the sync head at its current block until the next restart, whose backward sync fills the gap. Operators who see the error "in archive mode the sync head stays at its current block until a restart fills the gap" should restart eth-rpc. With `--eth-pruning <N>` there is no sync head and the index is in memory, so a restart does not help: the gap's blocks stay unindexed until they leave the retained window. No configuration changes are needed.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: patch
